  "authorNotes": "Scope: book chapters 4-11 plus the glossary. The Mohammadpur 2026 Class 3 Science final is a /50 paper covering chapters 6-11 only (it has no chapter 4 Matter or chapter 5 Energy questions, since MP set those in its half-yearly), so chapters 4-5 items come from MP Half-yearly 2026/2025 (MP_OTHER) and a few from the book. Every in-scope MP 2026 item was reused: all 5 MCQs (one reworded to the book's 'about three of four parts'), all 5 fill-ins, all 5 matching pairs and both distractors, 3 of the 5 one-sentence items, all 5 short answers and all 4 descriptive items (marks raised from 5 to 6). Two MP 2026 one-sentence items were not used: 'মাটি কী কী উপাদান দিয়ে তৈরি' (the matching row already gives that answer away) and the second force/shape example item (chapter 6 already has one). Mohammadpur never sets true/false for Class 3 Science, so the 10 true/false items are new from the book (5 true, 5 false, one per chapter, two for chapters 4 and 7). The glossary is covered by two one-sentence items (যোগাযোগ, হিউমাস) and the অচৌম্বক পদার্থ definition. Doubts: (1) Duration '৩ ঘণ্টা' is an assumption — the syllabus does not state it and Mohammadpur's /50 paper was 1 h 30 min. (2) The descriptive row has no choice, as published; if the school wants 'যেকোনো ৫টি', add items. (3) Two descriptive items are both from chapter 7 (water) because both are Mohammadpur 2026 items; swap s7-4 for a chapter 10 item (safe use of pen/TV/computer) if the owner prefers wider coverage. (4) The book itself contradicts the colour of loam soil (table says black, text says ash-grey), so no question asks it."
